g time coming and it's  one of the most satisfying and rewarding  moments in the entire naruto series for  so long naruto has been the underdog  starting off as the noisy annoying kid  who dreamt of becoming hokage naruto is  not exactly endeared himself to a lot of  people  along the way he found no shortage of  rivals was always a step behind his own  teammate sasuke and just seemed to be  delusional  becoming holgangi was nothing but a pipe  dream for this dreamer nonetheless he  persevered and he never gave up on his  dream at this point in the story  the dream of becoming hakagi or getting  recognized by the village  had been put aside in favor of training  in order to stop pain and protect the  village  let's just say that he came back looking  nothing short of a hero it was a  glorious entrance to save  everyone and finally face off against  payne in a decisive battle  brandishing his newly attained sage form  naruto was able to come out on top and  fight pain off the most cathartic part  of this is what happens afterwards  though  it's amazing to see him being showered  with love and finally becoming  everyone's hero  to take that haters we've come such a  long way and the hyperactive outcast has  finally become a hero  [Applause]  tv  next is takamura's rage against hawk the  whole arc with hawk is just one big  redemption tour for takamura  on second thought i think i've used  redemption to all wrong what is there to  redeem when takamura is already one of  the most awesome characters from hajime  no ippo  at that point in the story nevertheless  the arc just showcased the amount of  struggle thakamura had to go through in  order to chase his dreams  of conquering multiple weight classes  not making the first step on his journey  easy is his opponent  brian hawke the wbc junior middleweight  champion spends most of the arc in the  build-up to the eventual fight being a  thorn in the side of takamura first  showcasing his mettle against dakomula  in pre-fight confrontations before  acting all cocky in the lead-up to the  fight  this is a man that's continuously mocked  him and belittled all his efforts to  make it to the bout  seeing takamura just unleash his rage on  his opponent as well as the resulting  beatdown just feels so satisfying the  fight especially from this moment on is  just one of the best moments in ippo  and it gave me goosebumps to see  takamura finally get his one up on hall  [Music]  adaptation territory sword art online's  war of underworld gave us  gabrielle miller's death for most of war  of underworld we've been told to hate  this villain  it's no secret that sao villains are  almost always hate cigs but i doubt that  anyone can match gabriel miller in terms  of just sheer evil while the other guys  are just mostly memes that sexually  assault women we have here an actual  mass  murderer and a sociopath hiding  underneath a cold  calm facade you wouldn't expect that  this guy hired by the americans to steal  japanese research would have a  destructive fascination with the human  soul to the point of murdering his  childhood friend just to see her soul  the guy dying to kirito's attack that  was powered by the souls of literally  everyone in underworld was satisfying  enough but what comes next  is even better waking up as a ghost  after having physically died he finds  himself reunited with the childhood  friend that he murdered the upbeat  reunion would quickly turn ugly though  and he finally finds himself getting  dragged off to hell by none other than  the thousands of people that he killed  just for his sick  enjoyment it's a really scary way to go  but one that someone liked him deserved  yoshigangigira would be proud  in a somewhat similar scenario to the  last one we have yet another villain  being punished for his sins in maltese  punishment in  shield hero i don't know if malty's  worse than gabrielle miller but i'm  fairly certain about one thing  she feels more real and relevant i 